<title identifier="/us/usc/t99"><num value="99">Title 99</num><heading>Invented</heading>
<chapter identifier="/us/usc/t99/ch1"><num value="1">CHAPTER 1—</num><heading>WIDGETS</heading>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1"><num value="1">§ 1.</num><heading>Lists</heading>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/a"><num value="a">(a)</num><chapeau>In this chapter—</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/a/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>“widget” means a small device;</content></paragraph>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/a/2"><num value="2">(2)</num><content>“gadget” includes a widget.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/b"><num value="b">(b)</num><chapeau>The following rules apply:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/b/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>“widget” means a small device;</content></paragraph>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/b/2"><num value="2">(2)</num><content>“gadget” includes a widget.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/c"><num value="c">(c)</num><chapeau>As used in this chapter, the term—</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/c/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>“widget” means a small device;</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
</section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2"><num value="2">§ 2.</num><heading>Definitions</heading><chapeau>In this section:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><heading>Widget</heading><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s3"><num value="3">§ 3.</num><heading>A chapeau above a heading</heading>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s3/a"><num value="a">(a)</num><chapeau>For the purpose of this chapter—</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s3/a/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><heading>Widgets</heading>
<subparagraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s3/a/1/A"><num value="A">(A)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></subparagraph>
</paragraph>
</subsection>
</section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4"><num value="4">§ 4.</num><heading>Chapeaus with a lead-in</heading>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/a"><num value="a">(a)</num><chapeau>In this section, the following definitions apply:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/a/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/b"><num value="b">(b)</num><chapeau>In this section the following definitions shall apply:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/b/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/c"><num value="c">(c)</num><chapeau>In this chapter, unless the context otherwise requires—</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/c/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/d"><num value="d">(d)</num><chapeau>In this chapter and chapter 5:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/d/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/e"><num value="e">(e)</num><chapeau>In this subsection:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s4/e/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
</section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5"><num value="5">§ 5.</num><heading>Chapeaus that state no reach the rules read</heading>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5/a"><num value="a">(a)</num><chapeau>Except as otherwise provided, in this chapter:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5/a/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5/b"><num value="b">(b)</num><chapeau>In this chapter, the following terms have the following meanings:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5/b/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></paragraph>
</subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5/c"><num value="c">(c)</num><chapeau>In this section:</chapeau>
<paragraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5/c/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><chapeau>The following rules apply:</chapeau>
<subparagraph identifier="/us/usc/t99/s5/c/1/A"><num value="A">(A)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.</content></subparagraph>
</paragraph>
</subsection>
</section>
<section identifier="/us/usc/t99/s6"><num value="6">§ 6.</num><heading>Two definitions in one provision</heading>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s6/a"><num value="a">(a)</num><content>For purposes of this section, the term “zebra” means a striped widget.<proviso><i>Provided</i>, That every zebra is invented.</proviso>For purposes of this section, the term “apple” means a red widget.</content></subsection>
<subsection identifier="/us/usc/t99/s6/b"><num value="b">(b)</num><content>The term “widget” means a small device.<proviso><i>Provided</i>, That every widget is invented.</proviso>The term “widget” includes a gadget.</content></subsection>
</section>
